[2026-03-14T18:31:29.405Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NvmYh5xmFqDiN3quKb5pAT","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→     1→     1→# LinearClone Test Specification\n     2→     2→     2→\n     3→     3→     3→## Login Page (`/login`)\n     4→     4→     4→\n     5→     5→     5→**Components**: LoginForm\n     6→     6→     6→\n     7→     7→     7→### LoginForm\n     8→     8→     8→\n     9→     9→     9→#### Test: Login form renders with email and password fields\n    10→    10→    10→- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/login` (not authenticated)\n    11→    11→    11→- **Expected**: The page displays an email input field, a password input field, a \"Sign in\" button, and a \"Sign up\" link. The form has a clean, centered layout with the app branding.\n    12→    12→    12→\n    13→    13→    13→#### Test: Successful login with valid credentials\n    14→    14→    14→- **Initial state**: A user account exists with email \"user@test.com\" and password \"password123\"\n    15→    15→    15→- **Action**: User enters \"user@test.com\" in the email field, \"password123\" in the password field, and clicks the \"Sign in\" button\n    16→    16→    16→- **Expected**: User is redirected to `/my-issues`. A session token is stored in localStorage. The sidebar navigation is visible.\n    17→    17→    17→\n    18→    18→    18→#### Test: Login fails with invalid email\n    19→    19→    19→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    20→    20→    20→- **Action**: User enters \"nonexistent@test.com\" in the email field, \"password123\" in the password field, and clicks \"Sign in\"\n    21→    21→    21→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Invalid email or password\"). The user remains on the login page. No session token is stored.\n    22→    22→    22→\n    23→    23→    23→#### Test: Login fails with incorrect password\n    24→    24→    24→- **Initial state**: A user account exists with email \"user@test.com\". User is on `/login`.\n    25→    25→    25→- **Action**: User enters \"user@test.com\" in email, \"wrongpassword\" in password, and clicks \"Sign in\"\n    26→    26→    26→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Invalid email or password\"). The user remains on the login page.\n    27→    27→    27→\n    28→    28→    28→#### Test: Login form validates required fields\n    29→    29→    29→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    30→    30→    30→- **Action**: User clicks \"Sign in\" without entering email or password\n    31→    31→    31→- **Expected**: Validation errors are shown for both email and password fields indicating they are required.\n    32→    32→    32→\n    33→    33→    33→#### Test: Login form validates email format\n    34→    34→    34→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    35→    35→    35→- **Action**: User enters \"notanemail\" in the email field and clicks \"Sign in\"\n    36→    36→    36→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the email format is invalid.\n    37→    37→    37→\n    38→    38→    38→#### Test: Navigate to sign up page from login\n    39→    39→    39→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    40→    40→    40→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Sign up\" link\n    41→    41→    41→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/signup`.\n    42→    42→    42→\n    43→    43→    43→#### Test: Password field masks input\n    44→    44→    44→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    45→    45→    45→- **Action**: User types in the password field\n    46→    46→    46→- **Expected**: The input is masked (displayed as dots/bullets), the field type is \"password\".\n    47→    47→    47→\n    48→    48→    48→#### Test: Login form can be submitted via Enter key\n    49→    49→    49→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`, has entered valid email and password\n    50→    50→    50→- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the password field"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"s