→- **Action**: User enters \"user@test.com\" in email, \"wrongpassword\" in password, and clicks \"Sign in\"\n    26→    26→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Invalid email or password\"). The user remains on the login page.\n    27→    27→\n    28→    28→#### Test: Login form validates required fields\n    29→    29→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    30→    30→- **Action**: User clicks \"Sign in\" without entering email or password\n    31→    31→- **Expected**: Validation errors are shown for both email and password fields indicating they are required.\n    32→    32→\n    33→    33→#### Test: Login form validates email format\n    34→    34→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    35→    35→- **Action**: User enters \"notanemail\" in the email field and clicks \"Sign in\"\n    36→    36→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the email format is invalid.\n    37→    37→\n    38→    38→#### Test: Navigate to sign up page from login\n    39→    39→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    40→    40→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Sign up\" link\n    41→    41→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/signup`.\n    42→    42→\n    43→    43→#### Test: Password field masks input\n    44→    44→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    45→    45→- **Action**: User types in the password field\n    46→    46→- **Expected**: The input is masked (displayed as dots/bullets), the field type is \"password\".\n    47→    47→\n    48→    48→#### Test: Login form can be submitted via Enter key\n    49→    49→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`, has entered valid email and password\n    50→    50→- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the password field","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":970}}}
